{
  "description": "The `schedule_create` tool's arguments (ADR-SCH-01) against `ext/pipeshub/api/schedule-create-arguments.schema.json`: each language's validator (Node's chat route, the worker's check before it asks the person) must give `valid` for every case. Shape and lengths only; calendar dates, lead times, zones and cron semantics are checked in code.",
  "notes": [
    "The generated pydantic model accepts `notify: null` and a channel twice (datamodel-code-generator cannot express either), so those two cases are in these vectors and not in the schema's `.invalid.json`: a validator must check them against the JSON Schema, not the model alone."
  ],
